.TH AENIGMA-VPN-SERVER-CLIENT 8 "2026-08-13" "aenigma 5.0.0" "Aenigma Administration Scripts"
.SH NAME
aenigma-vpn-server-client \- issue an OpenVPN client certificate from
the Aenigma VPN server's CA
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aenigma-vpn-server-client
.B \-c
.I CLIENT_NAME
.B \-d
.I DOMAIN
.br
.B aenigma-vpn-server-client
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aenigma-vpn-server-client
issues a new client certificate, signed by the Easy-RSA certificate
authority previously initialized by
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8),
and assembles the certificate, key, CA certificate, and TLS
authentication key into a directory ready to be copied onto the
client machine for use with
.BR aenigma-vpn-client (8).
.PP
The script performs the following actions:
.IP \(bu 2
Verifies that
.I /etc/openvpn/easy\-rsa/pki/ca.crt
exists, and exits with an error if it does not, since a certificate
authority must already have been initialized by
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8)
before a client certificate can be issued.
.IP \(bu 2
Creates the client's directory,
.IR /etc/openvpn/clients/ CLIENT_NAME .
.IP \(bu 2
Generates a new certificate signing request for
.I CLIENT_NAME
(with no key passphrase) and signs it as a client certificate using
the CA.
.IP \(bu 2
Copies the CA certificate, the newly issued client certificate, and
the newly issued client private key into the client's directory,
restricting the private key's ownership to
.B openvpn:openvpn
and permissions to
.BR 700 .
.IP \(bu 2
Copies the TLS authentication key
.RI ( ta.key )
from the server directory for
.I DOMAIN
.RI ( /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN /ta.key)
into the client's directory, applying the same ownership and
permission restrictions.
.PP
The resulting directory,
.IR /etc/openvpn/clients/ CLIENT_NAME ,
is intended to be transferred to the client machine and placed at
the same relative path there, for consumption by
.BR aenigma-vpn-client (8).
.PP
.B aenigma-vpn-server-client
must be run as root, and is intended to be run on the VPN
.B server
host, not on a VPN client host.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " CLIENT_NAME"
Name identifying the client certificate to issue, e.g.
.IR john .
Used as the certificate common name and as the destination directory
name under
.IR /etc/openvpn/clients .
Required.
.TP
.BI \-d " DOMAIN"
Domain name of the already-configured VPN server (as set up by
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8))
whose TLS authentication key should be bundled with this client's
files. Required.
.TP
.B \-h
Display a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The client certificate was issued and its files assembled
successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid or missing arguments, the script was not run as root, the
CA has not yet been initialized, or an
.B easy-rsa
command failed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/openvpn/easy\-rsa/pki/
Existing Easy-RSA PKI directory; read to issue the new client
certificate. Not created by this script.
.TP
.I /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN /ta.key
Existing server TLS authentication key, copied into the client's
directory. Must already exist (created by
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8)).
.TP
.I /etc/openvpn/clients/ CLIENT_NAME /
Destination directory assembled by this script, containing
.IR ca.crt ,
.IR CLIENT_NAME .crt,
.IR CLIENT_NAME .key,
and
.IR ta.key .
This is the directory
.BR aenigma-vpn-client (8)
expects to already be present, at the same relative path, on the
client machine.
.SH EXAMPLES
Issue a client certificate named
.I john
for the server
.IR example.com :
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo aenigma-vpn-server-client \-c john \-d example.com
.EE
.RE
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
The client's private key and the copied TLS authentication key are
generated and assembled on the
.B server
host, with no passphrase, before being transferred elsewhere. The
transfer mechanism itself (how
.IR /etc/openvpn/clients/ CLIENT_NAME
is actually delivered to the client machine) is entirely outside the
scope of this script; it must be carried out over a channel that
itself protects this key material in transit, since the files are
plaintext, unencrypted private key material from the moment they are
created.
.SH NOTES
This script does not check whether a certificate or directory
already exists for the given
.I CLIENT_NAME
before running.
.B easy-rsa
may prompt, fail, or silently overwrite an existing request
depending on its own state and version; re-running this script for a
.I CLIENT_NAME
that was already issued a certificate should be treated as
potentially replacing that client's credentials, invalidating the
previously issued certificate and key pair for that name.
.PP
Client certificate revocation is not handled by this script, or, as
far as documented here, by any other Aenigma script; a client whose
access should be revoked requires manual
.B easy-rsa
CRL management outside this toolset.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR easyrsa (1),
.BR openvpn (8),
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8),
.BR aenigma-vpn-client (8)
